<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue id="9e57-4c1a-8b30-11a7" name="Gestalt" revision="1" battleScribeVersion="2.03" authorName="Homebrew" gameSystemId="5335-9d49-c85e-4817" gameSystemRevision="130" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <readme>Homebrew Gestalt codex for Warhammer 40,000 8th Edition. Requires the BSData "Warhammer 40,000 8th Edition" game system file. Points only; Power Level is not costed.</readme>
  <categoryEntries>
    <categoryEntry id="9e57-fac0-0000-0001" name="Faction: Gestalt" hidden="false"/>
  </categoryEntries>
  <rules>
    <rule id="9e57-0000-b463-01cd" name="Gestalt" hidden="false">
      <description>Reroll unit leadership tests and take the best result.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9e57-0000-d352-01ce" name="Noosphere" hidden="false">
      <description>Each GESTALT unit projects Shadow in the Warp to 16&quot;. Instances stack, to a maximum of -4 to psychic tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9e57-0000-f241-01cf" name="Operations Support" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll 1D6 on the Operations Support table at the start of each friendly turn for each full detachment, unless you are forced to redesignate a Gestalt Commander this turn. 1 - Interference Operations: declare 1 opponent stratagem; it may not be used during the current upcoming turn of both players. 2 - Disruption Strike: select 1 enemy unit; it suffers -1 to hit and halves its Move for the opponent's upcoming turn. 3 - Standoff Munitions: select 3 enemy units; each suffers 1D6 mortal wounds spread evenly across models. 4 - Orbital Precision Strike: select 1 enemy model; it suffers 2D6 S14 AP-4 D3 hits, each inflicting +1 mortal wound. 5 - Reinforcement Surge: select 1 friendly GESTALT INFANTRY unit; roll 1D3 and restore that many lost models. 6 - Shaping Operations: all friendly GESTALT units gain +1 Leadership until your next turn and may make an additional move at the end of the opponent's Movement phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9e57-0000-1130-01d0" name="Combined Arms" hidden="false">
      <description>GESTALT units do not suffer the penalty to hit rolls for firing Heavy weapons after making a normal move.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9e57-0000-301f-01d1" name="Gestalt Commander" hidden="false">
      <description>Any model with the GESTALT keyword may be designated as the Gestalt Commander at the start of any friendly turn. While designated, that model's unit gains the HQ battlefield role. On the turn of designation, the detachment the HQ belongs to may not roll on the Operations Support table. The Gestalt Commander does not award victory points from objectives such as Slay the Warlord.</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
